{
  "baseCommit": "a7dc460eaf7262a0cc96fb77f78f33eb35a16559",
  "boundaries": [
    "No production Java, POM, wire/disk catalog, resource limit, workflow or V5.2 experiment change. Native overlays are isolated diagnostics and are not committed as the runtime.",
    "Original missing ancestry, incomplete bridge propagation, occupied inactive generation, retain-all capacity exhaustion, and the extra-bridge fixture failure remain retained. The final explicit-pin diagnostic is separately source-bound.",
    "Only a volatile test registry records the genuine offline node endpoint. The successful native diagnostic is not durable pin tracking, autonomous election, full physical/history replay or Phase 3 acceptance.",
    "The finite model assumes atomic intent persistence, complete-copy observation and safe same-tip consolidation. Stable sizes 3/4/5 and eight delivery outcomes are tested; joint transitions, actual bytes, source/image lifetime, crash ordering and runtime performance remain open.",
    "Diagnostic inventory inspection verifies selected hashes, unchanged offline files, original applied-end ACK bytes and bridge endpoints/majorities. It does not reconstruct every original vote, application result or force order.",
    "Durable obligations before dispatch, uncertainty across restart/selection, authenticated state transfer, bounded maintenance, native cross-view contexts and complete 3C-3E are still required."
  ],
